 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The computation of features requires $O(1)$ operations per voxel for the 5 scalar properties, but involves calculating derivatives and determinants. The determinant calculation is constant time. The main cost is the derivative approximation which accesses neighboring voxels.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the original vector field and the computed feature volumes (5 scalar fields) if precomputed, or computing them on the fly. The source mentions GPU-based implementation for real-time performance [S1].
-*   **Measured Performance:** The method was implemented on an NVIDIA GeForce FX GPU to achieve interactive frame rates for steady and unsteady flow visualization [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Alleviates occlusion problems inherent in texture-based flow visualization by allowing distinct visual encoding of flow features. Can extract subtle features that 1D transfer functions miss.
-*   **Limitations:** Computationally expensive if full eigenanalysis were used (mitigated by using determinant). Requires careful tuning of 5 transfer functions.
-*   **When to use:** When visualizing complex 3D flow fields where occlusion is a problem and multiple flow characteristics (vorticity, divergence, etc.) need to be distinguished simultaneously.
-*   **When not to use:** When computational resources are extremely limited and real-time performance is critical without GPU acceleration, or when only simple velocity magnitude visualization is sufficient.
