 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Park, Budge, Linsen, Hamann, and Joy in 2004 [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of early flow visualization techniques like hedgehog plots, particle tracing, and streamlines, which present sparse, directed information. While texture-based approaches (like LIC and IBFV) gained popularity due to graphics hardware progress, they suffer from occlusion. This method combines feature-based extraction with texture-based rendering to provide global information while highlighting specific flow properties. It was demonstrated on the NVIDIA GeForce FX GPU [S1].
+The method was introduced by Park, Budge, Linsen, Hamann, and Joy in 2004 [S2]. It was developed to address the limitations of early flow visualization techniques like hedgehog plots, particle tracing, and streamlines, which present sparse, directed information [S2]. While texture-based approaches (like LIC and IBFV) gained popularity due to graphics hardware progress, they suffer from occlusion [S2]. This method combines feature-based extraction with texture-based rendering to provide global information while highlighting specific flow properties [S2]. It was demonstrated on the NVIDIA GeForce FX GPU [S2].
 
